WEBVTT

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.230
Welcome back, sir.

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:13.070
We've been waiting for you.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.360
Waiting for you.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.860
Come now, you must be tired.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.520
Have some tea while it's still warm.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.060
Have some.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.030
Wha... what...

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:35.360
What pretense is this, Masaru?

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.520
Can't you tell?

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.950
We're pretending to be maids.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.580
That's not what he meant...

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:44.420
What I mean by "pretense" is...

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:49.910
Why is it necessary to act like that towards me?

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:53.300
Oh, you're thinking too much into it, Tohma-kun.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:56.720
Tohma... kun...?

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.460
Be careful, Master.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.180
This smells dangerous.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.180
I-It's nothing really...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.790
Amazing.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.640
You figured it out just by smell!

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:07.390
Y-You idiot!

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:09.710
There's no point in hiding it.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.620
Even a mere child can figure out you have ulterior motives.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:13.360
Just say it.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.320
Well, about that...

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.740
Today at school...

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.570
"The names listed below must take a makeup exam tomorrow..."

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.200
Notice on Fixed Examination Results

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.200
The names listed below must take

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.200
a makeup exam tomorrow:

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.200
Daimon Masaru

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.070
I have a makeup exam?!

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:27.740
And it has to be tomorrow of all days...

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.650
Suffer the consequences if you run, Daimon.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.630
W-Wait a second!

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.630
I have something really important tomorrow...!

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.430
There's no use arguing.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:39.310
If you don't come, you'll have to repeat the year again.

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:44.060
...and that's what happened.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.390
Well, I can't.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.020
But I haven't even said anything yet!

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:57.240
Although I do have a Ph.D., I think it'll be impossible for me to teach you how to study.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:58.940
That's true.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:00.720
Yeah, it's impossible.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.700
This isn't about studying.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.910
Then what?

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:07.580
I have a favor... I want to ask of you.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.890
A favor?

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.340
The thing is, tomorrow is Chika's birthday.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:14.100
Chika...

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.500
That's your little sister, right?

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.420
Yeah, yeah! You remember well.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:23.100
Since I'm in this situation, could you take care of Chika for me until my test is over?

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.180
Just that?

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:26.930
You could ask Yoshino to do that!

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.000
I don't mind.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.070
The pay will be pretty expensive though.

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.930
Hey, don't say such weird things!

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.980
Oh, so are you going to do it for free?

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.100
W-Well...

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.650
It can't be Yoshino.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:41.570
I need someone who can act as the father.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.740
So... please.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.160
Please be a part of my family tomorrow, for one day.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.080
Family...

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.470
Why do I have to come to your house now?

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.800
The birthday's tomorrow.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.030
Chika’s tough to deal with, so we’ll have to see if she’s okay with it first.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:08.000
This doesn't mean I've accepted your request yet.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.770
Anyway, come on in.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:11.510
We're home!

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:14.810
Welcome!

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.610
I'm Tohma H. Norstein.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:20.030
Sorry for my impoliteness the other day when we met at my car.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.580
Same here.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:23.670
Thank you for taking care of Masaru.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:24.820
N-Not at all.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:25.740
Chika!

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:29.990
Tohma said he'd hang out with you on your birthday tomorrow, in my place.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:30.750
Isn't that great?

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:32.290
Really?!

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:34.630
All right! I'm so happy!

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:35.880
No... um...

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.320
I'm still...

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.170
But...

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.630
It's not a bother, is it?

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.370
I, Tohma H. Norstein,

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:51.010
will put my entire heart and soul into producing Chika-chan's birthday!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.560
Tohma-kun!

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.230
Thank you!

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.070
Oh, hey!

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.200
Do you have someone like Agu-chan, Tohma-kun?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.960
Agu-chan...

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.030
Oh, you mean a partner!

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.940
He's called Gaomon.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.690
Hey, show me, show me!

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:13.630
Sure.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.770
Gaomon, Realize!

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.710
Yes, Master!

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:22.620
He's so cute!

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.610
N-Nice to meet you.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.300
It's a dog, a dog, a talking dog!

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.180
She called you a dog!

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.490
I'm not a dog.

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:33.370
I'll start preparing dinner.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.890
Then we'll take our leave.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:39.010
You should eat with us, Tohma-kun!

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:41.860
Thank you, but I still have work to do...

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.570
Don't hold back. Stay and eat with us.

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:47.530
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.240
Here!

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:51.200
Gao-chan, open wide!

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.030
Hey, you took my share!

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:56.720
No, I didn't.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:59.250
What’s in your mouth right now is mine!

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:58.490
This is a lively dining table.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.900
Bastard, stop eating more!

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.100
Tohma.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.000
Tohma!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:12.760
Something wrong?

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:15.230
Does the food not suit your tastes?

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.330
That's not it at all!

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.460
I'm just...

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:28.610
Just not used to this sort of atmosphere.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.540
Thank you for the meal.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.990
I'll be going now.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.670
Let's go, Gaomon.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:39.770
Master!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.480
Hey, Tohma!

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:47.970
Don't worry.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:51.800
I'll keep my promise for you and your family.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:01.020
What happened to him?

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.130
10 AM:  Meet with the Daimon family at their house.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:16.260
12 PM:  Have lunch at the hotel's top-floor restaurant.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:20.970
After that, shop for a birthday present at the hotel's brand shop,

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:24.490
stroll through the Japanese garden, and have afternoon tea.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:27.670
3PM:  Horseback riding at a club.

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:33.390
And at 6PM, meet up again with Masaru and have dinner at a French restaurant.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.890
Lunch (Top-floor Restaurant)

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.890
Birthday present in a brand shop

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.890
Strolling through a Japanese Garden

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.890
Afternoon Tea

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.890
Horseback Riding club

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.890
Dinner (Tower Hotel)

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:35.890
It's perfect.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:38.580
All of the reservations are in order.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:39.350
This will be called...

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:43.980
<b>The Magnificent Birthday Plan</b>

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:43.650
The Magnificent Birthday Plan.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.590
Tohma's Day Off

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.590
Exploding BomberNanimon

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:50.760
Tohma's Day Off!

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:52.340
Exploding BomberNanimon!

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:59.070
He's late. What is he doing?

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:02.310
Oh, here he comes.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:05.770
You’re late, Tohma!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.310
Happy birthday, Chika-chan.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:19.450
Thank you!

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:25.420
I promise today will be a wonderful day you’ll never forget.

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:26.770
Okay.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.380
I’m looking forward to it.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:31.040
Thank you, Tohma-kun.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:33.420
We’ll be in your care for today.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:34.920
Please leave it to me.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.470
Also... this is for you, Sayuri-san.

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:41.090
Oh, for me too?

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.680
It’s not even my birthday.

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.140
This is my thanks for yesterday’s meal.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.760
I don’t really get it, but...

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.110
It looks like you’re highly motivated.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:53.270
I told you, I’m a man who keeps his word.

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:54.530
That’s true...

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:55.560
Masaru!

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:58.280
It’s time for you to get to school.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.570
Ah, that’s right!

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:03.810
I’ll be off to my exams then, Tohma.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.210
I’m counting on you.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:06.920
Leave it to me.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:09.630
See ya!

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:14.610
We should get going as well.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:16.110
First, at the hotel’s lounge, there's...

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.990
I have a place I want to go to!

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:19.970
Can I?

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.240
Of course!

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:24.130
You can do what you please!

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:25.930
All right!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.010
The schedule’s already in ruins...

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.740
This was beyond my calculations...

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:42.760
Turn right over there, then left at the second corner.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.580
What should I do to recover...?

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:50.290
Is something wrong?

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.210
No, nothing...

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.500
Hey, what’s wrong?

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.970
My apologies, Tohma-sama.

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:05.860
What are you doing?

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:08.260
The roads are rather narrow, so...

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:11.000
That’s okay, it’s close by here.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.480
Let’s get out and walk!

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:16.400
Now we can’t even use the car...

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.540
Tohma-kun, hurry up!

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.120
Today’s Make-up Exams

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.120
Modern Japanese Language

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.120
English

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.120
Japanese history

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.120
Physics

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.120
Mathematics

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:24.370
English Make-up Problems

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:24.370
Name     DAIMON MASARU

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:27.340
I have no idea.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:34.000
Game Star

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:31.390
This is where you wanted to go?

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:32.680
Yeah! Let’s go!

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:36.620
Tohma-kun, hurry up!

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:37.970
I’ll be right there.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:40.720
Hello?

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:43.500
This is Tohma H. Norstein.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.930
I’m sorry, please cancel my reservations.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:51.400
Request whichever you want.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:52.100
Really?

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.090
Then...

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.040
That one!

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:56.520
Roger.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:01.450
Got it.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.450
Oh, not that one...

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.290
Oh... that one...

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.180
Yay!

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:14.740
Chika, you’re so good at games.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:18.460
I... lost...

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.160
She’s strong.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:23.180
She’s completely different from Masaru the machine-breaker, isn’t she, Master?

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:27.430
No, she ambushed me at angles beyond my calculations...

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:30.240
She truly is Masaru’s younger sister.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:37.260
I wonder if Tohma’s doing all right...

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.490
Daimon! Don’t look away!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.350
I’m hungry.

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:46.910
It’s almost lunchtime.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.580
Okay, now I’ll move things according to plan...

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.790
If you’d like, there’s a French place I know...

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.790
I know a good place!

00:11:57.380 --> 00:12:15.850
{The older brother left home to go to school, which was 2km away from his house.
10 minutes later, the younger sister chased after him using the same road.
The older brother walks 80m per minute, while the sister runs 200m per minute.
Use equations to determine how many minutes it will take for the sister to reach her brother.}

00:11:58.390 --> 00:12:02.490
"The older brother left home to go to school, which was 2km away from his house."

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.970
"10 minutes later, the younger sister chased after him using the same road."

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:12.360
"The older brother walks 80m per minute, while the sister runs 200m per minute."

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.850
"Use equations to determine how many minutes it will take for the sister to reach her brother."

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:22.050
The older brother should just wait for her.

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:26.030
Monjayaki

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:32.000
NOTE: <i>Monjayaki</i> (もんじゃ焼き) is fried pancake batter with cabbage and other ingredients, like okonomiyaki, but more liquid-like.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.660
This is food...?

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:36.920
Do you know how to eat it?

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:38.130
Er, no...

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:41.840
Press it down like this, then...

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.640
Delicious!

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:50.070
This sure hits the spot.

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:53.050
Chika really loves her monjayaki.

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:54.350
Tohma-kun, have some!

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:55.780
O-Okay...

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:00.060
It’s good!

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.280
That was a great meal!

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:05.010
Master, please give me the bill!

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:05.990
Yes, sir!

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:09.330
That’ll be 1740 yen.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.990
I’ll be paying with this.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.940
Are you joking?

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:16.960
We don’t accept anything but cash!

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:21.460
I’m... not holding any cash on me...

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:24.100
I’m really sorry about that, Sayuri-san.

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:25.730
It was the least I could do.

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:28.430
You’re doing enough watching over Chika.

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:33.190
Everything’s been falling away from the Magnificent Birthday Plan.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:36.430
No, I must recover somehow!

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:41.400
Chika-chan, if there’s any other place you’d like to go to, go ahead and request it.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:45.020
I want to see fireworks!

00:13:45.020 --> 00:13:47.360
Ones that make a big bang and light up really bright!

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:55.750
An amusement park?

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:57.160
Cool!

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:00.600
They have a fireworks display here at nighttime.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:01.540
Really?

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:05.590
Let’s have fun at the attractions before the fireworks start.

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:39.240
Wow... it’s beautiful...

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:41.520
Look Mom!

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:44.710
Do you think our house is over there?

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:45.960
Let’s see...

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:04.640
Tohma-kun!

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:06.400
Is something wrong?

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:08.740
Are you not having fun?

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:10.590
Just the opposite!

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.450
I haven’t had this much fun in a long time.

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:17.540
Fireworks? They’ve already started?

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:18.370
No...

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:20.240
This is a Digimon!

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:28.520
Look and be surprised, you bastards!

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:38.510
BomberNanimon

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:38.510
Adult Level

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:30.150
BomberNanimon.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.740
An Adult Level Digimon whose entire body is a bomb.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:38.510
His special attack is Freethrow Bomb. It can explode anything surrounding him.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:40.330
Here!

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:45.290
Will you be all right, Tohma-kun?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.520
Please get away from here!

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:50.490
I’d also appreciate it if you could direct the others in finding shelter.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:52.200
Tohma-kun!

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:54.150
Don’t worry.

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:56.160
After all, this is my job.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:00.050
It’s dangerous over there!

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.980
Damn it...

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:08.450
I haven’t even granted all of Chika-chan’s wishes to her satisfaction yet...

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:19.760
You’re gonna get hurt, you bastard!

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:21.430
It’s him...

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:22.850
Master!

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:23.510
Yeah!

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:27.400
Gaomon, Realize!

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:31.360
Yes, Master!

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:35.530
Master, what are your orders?

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.880
Isn’t it obvious?

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:39.000
This is Tohma.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:42.040
There’s a Digimon rampaging in Area U-308.

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:46.660
The target is one BomberNanimon. I request the area to be shutdown.

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:47.970
Digimon signal confirmed.

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:50.110
Area U-308 will be blockaded.

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:53.720
Tohma, standby and wait for the others.

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:57.430
I’m sorry, sir, but this is personal.

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:58.680
What?

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.100
What do you mean, Tohma?

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:03.070
Let’s go, Gaomon.

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:04.230
Yes, Master!

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:07.190
Chika-chan and Sayuri-san...

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:08.190
I will protect you!

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:14.240
Digisoul Charge!

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:18.910
Gaomon, evolve!

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:30.110
<b>mou nani mo nai sekai ja kandou dekinai</b>

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:30.110
<b>A world that's full of nothing can't inspire anyone</b>

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:35.070
<b>sou, kizuita sono hi kara wakaru no sa</b>

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:35.070
<b>You'll understand what I mean after the day you realize that</b>

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.580
Gaogamon!

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.180
<b>furue wo tomete</b>

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.180
<b>Stop your trembling</b>

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:40.800
<b>hitomi wo hirake</b>

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:40.800
<b>Open your eyes</b>

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.390
Finish it in one minute!

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:40.760
Go!

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:45.610
<b>kimi no jikan wo tokihanate!</b>

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:45.610
<b>And liberate your time!</b>

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:46.830
Take that!

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:49.570
<b>mirai e Shootin' star!</b>

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:49.570
<b>Oh shootin' star to the future!</b>

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:52.860
<b>hikari no aachi egake</b>

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:52.860
<b>Draw an arch of light</b>

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:58.130
<b>todoku no sa shinjitsuzukeru naraba</b>

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:58.130
<b>As long as you keep believing, it'll reach up there</b>

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:55.320
Good!

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:57.200
Now take him down with one strike!

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:03.930
<b>kimi wo yobu koe ga kokoro de hajiketara</b>

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:03.930
<b>When the voice that calls you bellows with the heart</b>

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.950
You’ll all be...

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:03.160
blown to bits along with me, you bastard!

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:10.100
<b>subete ga hajimaru Believer!</b>

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:10.100
<b>That's when everything will begin, Believer!</b>

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:06.700
Outta my way, bastard!

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:11.080
Move!

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:11.710
Master!

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:13.340
Damn it...

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:18.800
If that load of bombs detonated, it wouldn’t just be fireworks but a sea of fire!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.420
<i>I want to see fireworks!</i>

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:24.760
<i>Ones that make a big bang and light up really bright!</i>

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:26.580
That's it!

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.830
<b>You can be a shootin' star!</b>

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.830
<b>You can be a shootin' star!</b>

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.210
<b>sore ga kimi no yakusoku</b>

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.210
<b>That is your promise</b>

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:30.650
Gaogamon! Along with those bombs...

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:32.700
Throw him...

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:36.220
<b>kurayami wo kirisakeru sono chikara</b>

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:36.220
<b>The power to tear the darkness to pieces</b>

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:33.610
Up into the sky!

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:35.140
Yes, Master!

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:42.190
<b>omoi no tsuyosa ga supiido ageru kara</b>

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:42.190
<b>The strength of your feelings will raise your speed</b>

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:48.130
<b>sono mama tobunda Believer!</b>

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:48.130
<b>So fly on as you are, Believer!</b>

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:50.370
<b>mirai e Shootin' star!</b>

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:50.370
<b>Oh shootin' star to the future!</b>

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:53.660
<b>hikari no aachi egake</b>

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:53.660
<b>Draw an arch of light</b>

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:58.930
<b>todoku no sa shinjitsuzukeru naraba</b>

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:58.930
<b>As long as you keep believing, it'll reach up there</b>

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:55.340
Now!

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:57.500
Spiral Blow!

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:04.730
<b>kimi wo yobu koe ga kokoro de hajiketara</b>

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:04.730
<b>When the voice that calls you bellows with the heart</b>

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:04.270
I’ll let you off easy this time, you bastard!

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:10.900
<b>subete ga hajimaru Believer!</b>

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:10.900
<b>That's when everything will begin, Believer!</b>

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:20.740
Fire department!

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:21.870
Call the fire department!

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:22.790
We've completed the evacuation.

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:24.740
Wait!

00:19:24.980 --> 00:19:25.880
Hurry, hurry!

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:27.880
Stay back!

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:31.000
Please stay back! Stay back!

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.440
Please don't get too close!

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:47.000
I finally...

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.250
finished...

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:56.900
Tohma-kun!

00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.750
I’m sorry...

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:03.070
It doesn’t look like we’ll be able to see the fireworks like this.

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.050
What are you talking about?

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:08.280
You launched those fireworks we just saw, didn’t you?

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:11.230
Tohma-kun, Tohma-kun!

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:13.670
What is it?

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:16.620
You know, the fireworks were really pretty!

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:17.420
Thank you!

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:25.360
I’ve gotten hungry.

00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:26.650
So have I.

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:29.510
Then, there’s a French restaurant I know...

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:31.020
This is my thanks for the fireworks.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:35.190
I’d love for you to eat plenty of my home-cooking today!

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:37.270
Y-Yes, ma’am!

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:43.820
Happy birthday, Chika-chan

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:47.280
Happy birthday!

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:50.740
This is a present from us.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:52.750
Yoshino and I chose it together.

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:54.610
Thanks!

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:55.210
Chika.

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:57.140
I’m really sorry.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:59.920
I promised to spend all day with you today...

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:04.030
Today was really fun!

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.630
Right, Tohma-kun?

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:10.620
Really? That’s good to hear.

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:12.420
You jerk! Those are my fried eggs!

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:14.260
Whoever grabs it first gets to eat it.

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:21.150
This is delicious!

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:24.390
Damn it, Tohma! You took advantage of the confusion!

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:25.410
Oh, give it up.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:28.220
Not all of Sayuri-san’s fried eggs belong to you.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.730
What?!

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:32.580
Masaru-niichan, stop embarrassing me!

